message.content:
Below is a **minimal, self‑contained example** that shows how to create a “flip‑on‑hover” card using only CSS (no JavaScript).  
Feel free to copy the HTML/CSS into your own project and tweak the dimensions, colors, or content as you wish.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card wrapper – gives perspective ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:160px;
    perspective:800px;          /* Needed for 3D effect */
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Inner container – holds front/back faces ---------- */
.card-inner {
    position:relative;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    text-align:center;
    transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* Keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Hover trigger ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* Rotate around Y‑axis */
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣  Front face ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;       /* Hide backside when turned away */
    border-radius:12px;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    font-family:sans-serif;
    font-size:1.2rem;
    color:white;
}

.card-front {
    background:#3498db;               /* Front side colour */
}

.card-back {
    background:#e74c3c;               /* Back side colour */
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* Start rotated so it’s hidden initially */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <div class="card-front">Front Side</div>
        <div class="card-back">Back Side</div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| 1 | `perspective` on `.card` | Gives depth to the 3D transformation. |
| 2 | `.card-inner` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps its child elements (`.card-front`, `.card-back`) in 3D space. |
| 3 | `backface-visibility: hidden` on both faces | Hides the back of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| 4 | On hover, `.card-inner` gets `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Rotates the whole inner container, flipping the card. |
| 5 | `.card-back` starts rotated 180° | Positions the back face directly behind the front, ready to appear when the container flips. |

#### Customisation tips

- Change `width` / `height` of `.card` to resize the card.
- Replace the background colours with images or gradients.
- Add more content inside `.card-front` / `.card-back` (text, icons, etc.).
- If you want a flip along the X‑axis instead, replace `rotateY(180deg)` with `rotateX(180deg)` everywhere.

That’s all you need! 🎉

